# Prettier ignore for nyuchi/.github.

# Standard ignores
node_modules/
.git/

# Files with structural meaning that Prettier would harm
LICENSE
CODEOWNERS
CODEOWNERS.example
.github/CODEOWNERS

# YAML is handled by yamllint and actionlint, not Prettier — they have
# stronger guarantees about GitHub Actions semantics that Prettier does
# not understand (e.g. the `on:` truthy quirk).
*.yml
*.yaml

# Governance documents are authored by the Founder as legal / formal
# documents. Prettier's markdown formatter reflows numbered paragraphs
# ("2.2 The company pursues...") after a list as loose list-item
# continuations, which corrupts the document's structure. Hand-format
# these files.
profile/governance/

# Lockfiles, generated output
*-lock.json
*-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPO-SPECIFIC ADDITION, everything above this line is the canonical
# nyuchi/.github .prettierignore verbatim.
#
# siafudb-kuzu is a fork of KuzuDB v0.11.3 and carries a large vendored
# upstream corpus that this repository does not author:
#
#  - third_party/ is vendored source (brotli and friends), each carrying
#    its own project's house style. Restyling it would be rewriting
#    someone else's project and would conflict with every future
#    upstream merge.
#  - The dataset/ and extension/ fixture trees are NOT single JSON
#    documents. Delta Lake _delta_log/*.json are newline-delimited BY
#    SPECIFICATION, the Iceberg .gz.metadata.json files are gzipped
#    despite the extension, and dataset/json-error/ is a directory of
#    deliberately malformed inputs whose invalidity is the thing under
#    test. Prettier cannot parse them and should not try.
#  - tools/rust_api/kuzu-src is a symlink to the repository root, which
#    the Rust crate needs in order to vendor the C++ sources. A ** glob
#    follows it and walks the whole tree again through ever-longer paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/
tools/rust_api/kuzu-src/
# The whole test corpus: dataset descriptions from SNAP, LDBC and LSQB, and
# the extension fixture trees. Same rationale as .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc and
# .jsonlintignore - these three files exclude exactly the same content, so
# there is one answer to "is this ours?" rather than three.
dataset/
extension/*/test/
